<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n68662" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μονό-στροφος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>consisting of a single
				strophe</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στροφή</span>
				Sch.Tricl.<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				239
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φως</span> ibid.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅμαξα μ.</span> either a cart <i>with
				solid wheels</i>, or <i>wheelbarrow</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				5.7.6
			</span></i>; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μονόκυκλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>of one turn</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕλιξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Speus.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Procl.
				<u>in Euc.</u>
				pp.180,187
			</span></i> F., <i><span class="en">
				Papp.
				1110.2
			</span></i>.</div>
